 "_comment": "ids: the stable u16 id table for core records (index = id); append only, never reorder. Tile-anchored decorations (view/actors/dressing_view.gd). id -> model (res:// literal, fetched by tools/fetch_assets.sh), footprint [w, h] in tiles (the cells it covers, left-bottom at the record's x, y), anchor (ground: stands on the solid tile below its footprint; ceiling: hangs under the solid tile above it), fit_h (height above the model's origin, in tiles, it is scaled to: robust to packs cooked in cm), z (its plane, in tiles: negative behind the actors at 0, positive in front; terrain blocks span -0.5..0.5), depth (z squash, so a round tree does not poke through the terrain front face), jitter (random scale +-, per placement), lod (which of a Synty model's LOD meshes to draw: some of the nature packs' LOD0 trees run to 30000 triangles), gap (columns to the next object in this pass, if wider than the footprint: a tree stands on one column of a slope and keeps its distance), where (biomes, band surface | cave, on: tile names it may stand on or hang from), weight (relative frequency for scatter), tint (hex, optional), textures ({material name: png or #hex colour, or * for untextured materials: png}: restores an atlas a cooked file lost). Records are {id, x, y}; tiles stay the truth. Places pieces (band \"place\"; never scattered): still (no random yaw), turn (degrees of yaw), anchor wall (hangs on a back wall: every footprint cell open with a background wall). Placed by PlaceBuilder through data/places/kits.json.",
